<title>USA: Eagle completes $35.2 mln securitization.</title>
<headline>Eagle completes $35.2 mln securitization.</headline>
<dateline>GURNEE, Ill. 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eagle Finance Corp, a specialized financial services company, said Wednesday it completed a $35.2 million securitization of non-prime automobile receivables through Greenwich Capital Markets Inc.</p>
<p>President Robert Braasch in a statement said the securitization &quot;enhances Eagle's operating flexibility through access to a large and growing funding source.&quot;</p>
<p>Braasch also said Eagle recently increased to $80 million its loan sale program with General Electric Capital Corp, a General Electric Co unit, and renegotiated and extended through June 1997 its revolving credit agreement with nine commercial banks.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
